    {
      "source": "vvaharness/orchestrator/checkpoints.py",
      "line_start": 68,
      "line_end": 68,
      "text": "Whether an S4 checkpoint has no unit left in an unresolved failure state; False means --resume must not reuse it.",
      "context": "literal string"
    },
    {
      "source": "vvaharness/orchestrator/checkpoints.py",
      "line_start": 101,
      "line_end": 115,
      "text": "The model/via/config a detection stage's checkpoint was ACTUALLY produced\n    under, plus that stage's own token bucket.\n\n    Checkpoints are keyed ``(run_id, step)`` with no model/via/config column\n    (``store.py``'s ``checkpoints`` table), so resuming stage N under a\n    DIFFERENT ``--config`` than produced it left the manifest attributing N's\n    model/tokens to whatever the CURRENT config's role_models/TOKENS say —\n    misattributing route and dropping the original spend. Saved as a SECOND\n    checkpoint row per stage (``<step>_prov``, via ``save_ckpt``/``load_ckpt``\n    themselves — same pattern as :data:`REPO_IDENTITY_STEP`, no new storage\n    mechanism and no ``store.py`` schema change) so a cached stage's manifest\n    row can report the truth it was actually computed under. A stage with no\n    ``_prov`` row (written before this existed) has no envelope to read and\n    falls back to today's behaviour — see ``load_stage_provenance``.\n    ",
      "context": "literal string"
    },
